Hi all,

As our traditional launch date is Haloween, we're now one month away from this
year's Tournament start.  Now is the time we usually post this announcement,
and a request for folks to volunteer servers for the Tournament.

This year, however, we're going to need more than the usual amount of help. ;-)

Since Matt is starting his first term as a real professor this fall, and I'm in
the middle of a major remodelling project on the house my fiance and I managed
to buy last year, we're going to need a lot of help if we're going to get the
(clearly needed) changes made to the Tournament system for this year.

As you may recall, our placements have always been based on the raw NetHack
score which was pretty clearly demonstrated last year to turn the game into
basically a contest of patience among the folks who get to the Astral Plane.
It was also demonstrated to be a bit of a pain in the neck, since it turns out
to be possible to overflow NetHack's score counter and cause it to log a
negative score.

After much discussion, we decided to scrap all but the single "Highest Score"
trophy and move to other more interesting ways of choosing winners based
largely on conducts.

To do this, though, we're going to need a few more Perl programmers, since
neither Matt nor I can really get the time this month to do it ourselves.  Most
of the Tournament system is still usable (account management; backups; game
recording; score/record file management) but the part that actually creates the
scoreboard will need to be totally re-written and we'll need someone familiar
with the conducts to help guarantee that our game servers are logging
everything we'll need (since the norml NetHack doesn't log any of this).

So, are any of y'all up for helping to come up with a suitable patched NetHack
binary to monitor and log this stuff and re-write the Tournament scoring system
to use it?

Thanks,
-robin

